 <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae. </italic></article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1996</year><volume>133</volume><fpage>1017</fpage><lpage>1026</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8655575</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>DNW</given-names></name><name><surname>Barondes</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence for export of a muscle lectin from cytosol to extracellular matrix and for a novel secretory mechanism</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1990</year><volume>110</volume><fpage>1681</fpage><lpage>1691</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2335567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorta</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferreira</surname><given-names>AT</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshiro</surname><given-names>MEM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshida</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> signal  induced by <italic>Trypanosoma cruzi</italic>metacyclic trypomastigote surface molecules implicated in mammalian cell invasion</article-title><source>Mol Biochem Parasitol</source><year>1995</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>289</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8577342</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Florkiewicz</surname><given-names>RZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Majack</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Buechler</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Florkiewicz</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantitative export of FGF-2 occurs through an alternative, energy-dependent non-ER/Golgi pathway</a